{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition","id":1488463,"title":"Is Ur-Shurgi the most hated in VTM or is there competition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-30T09:44:25-07:00","id":1488463,"title":"Is Ur-Shurgi the most hated in VTM or is there competition?","content":"I'm just curious as he can't be the only misfire that this series created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T10:20:37-07:00","id":1488464,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's plenty of worse ideas but I almost dread bringing them up.<br /> <br /> I mean...<br /> <br /> Himmler of the Sabbat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T10:23:05-07:00","id":1488465,"title":"","content":"The title seems a little click-baity, but I'll bite.<br /> <br /> Are you basing this idea on actual evidence, or is it more of an assumption? I don't hate Ur-Shulgi at all. But then, scary-OP Methuselahs are one of the things I like about VtM.<br /> <br /> I can maybe think of a few particular facets of characters that I hate (a few Ventrue with some decidedly WTF feeding requirements come to mind), but I don't know if I could name a single character that I just absolutely hate in the entire canon. Mind you, there's lots of stuff I haven't read yet, maybe they're out there somewhere.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, I forgot about Berlin By Night. I still dunno if I'd quite use the word &quot;hate,&quot; but excellent point from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>. *shudders*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 07-30-2022, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T10:31:21-07:00","id":1488466,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by most hated? In universe? I would say either Harold Zettler, A Board of Director of Pentex, a Malkavian 5th Gen. Who also created a whole path of Dark Thaumaturgy, which allows you to host a Maeljin Incarna at the highest level. <br /> <br /> Or Shaitan, who is also a good candidate for the most hated in universe. Along with...Nurgal? I think, I am rusty in VTM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T10:42:25-07:00","id":1488469,"title":"","content":"the whole of clan baali?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T12:03:37-07:00","id":1488477,"title":"","content":"<b>Is Ur-Shulgi actually hated or loved to hate?</b><br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi is a character that is probably the most <i>controversial</i> in V:TM with the possible exception of Sabbat Lucita. I wouldn't say that he's universally hated, though. There's also the difference between &quot;hate&quot; and &quot;love to hate&quot; which I drew as a distinction in the NPC thread and might have inspired this thread.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi is a ten ton wrecking ball to most campaigns if you introduce him and your only ways of doing so are either as a presence the PCs are never going to encounter or something that NPCs have to deal with (I.E. Transylvania Chronicles). The PCs will possibly hear of him from Banu Haqim defectors or deal with Ur-Shulgi's cultists. He's a character that may be an enemy if they're Banu Haqim themselves but you're not ever going to get into a fist-fight with him.<br /> <br /> However, it's also possible to deal with Ur-Shulgi. I mentioned the Transylvania Chronicles where you encounter people like Tremere, Kupala, and Yorak. Now, you'll never get into a fist fight with<br /> Ur-Shulgi but maybe you can do a campaign about finding Ur-Shulgi's true name, getting the help of an Archdemon to kill him, or even beseeching Haqim to whoop his ass. Which basically means Ur-Shulgi is Sauron. Sauron can't be beaten in a fist fight, Isildur aside. No, you need to find the Macguffin and tossing the object into a volcano. Any reasonable vampire campaign dealing with Ur-Shulgi has to have you as the Hobbits and that's not something most vampires are up to doing.<br /> <br /> As a background element, Ur-Shulgi also kind of wrecks the background of more lower stakes vampire games because he confirms Gehenna is real and that vampire demigods can pop up at any time.<br /> <br /> But SOME people like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T12:23:01-07:00","id":1488480,"title":"","content":"Ur-Shulgi is a perfectly fine character if an ST actually wants to run a Gehenna chronicle where the PCs roleplay out the beginning of the end of the world and thus the the beginning of the destruction of the actual game setting itself. Which is what the Revised Developer Justin Achilli wanted the setting to be.<br /> <br /> He's a terrible character to exist in any chronicle that is NOT about Gehenna and the end of the world.<br /> <br /> The problem is that most STs and players do NOT want their chronicles to be about Gehenna and the destruction of the game's setting. They want a stable Camarilla. They want the Sabbat to be recognizably Sabbat. They want all the toys to remain the toybox so they can keep using them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this was not limited to Ur-Shulgi. Revised introduced a lot of concepts that simply harm the setting if it is not a Gehenna style chronicle where everything breaks down. If Gehenna is going to happen, then major things like the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla en masse, the Sabbat wiping out entire Paths of Enlightenment, destroying the True Black Hand, Revenant families defecting to the Camarilla, Tremere leaving his body and wiping out all the Tremere anti-tribu in the ritual to do so, etc. are all fine ideas. They give a very strong sense that things are breaking down. In such a world, the Masquerade is going to break down. Which is not that much of a problem because human society will start to self-destruct too since Gehenna is just one aspect of the end of the world. The very concept of this chronicle requires the setting become something unrecognizable. That can be a very intriguing, fascinating, and fun chronicle.<br /> <br /> But if people just want Gehenna to be a looming threat that may or may not happen in the near or distant future, and they want to keep all the toys in the toybox to use again and again, then all of these concepts from Revised are just terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T13:43:23-07:00","id":1488487,"title":"","content":"Interesting, probably my favorite NPC after Saulot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T16:19:51-07:00","id":1488503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488480#post1488480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ur-Shulgi is a perfectly fine character if an ST actually wants to run a Gehenna chronicle where the PCs roleplay out the beginning of the end of the world and thus the beginning of the destruction of the actual game setting itself. Which is what the Revised Developer Justin Achilli wanted the setting to be.<br /> <br /> He's a terrible character to exist in any chronicle that is NOT about Gehenna and the end of the world.<br /> <br /> The problem is that most STs and players do NOT want their chronicles to be about Gehenna and the destruction of the game's setting. They want a stable Camarilla. They want the Sabbat to be recognizably Sabbat. They want all the toys to remain in the toybox so they can keep using them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this was not limited to Ur-Shulgi. Revised introduced a lot of concepts that simply harm the setting if it is not a Gehenna-style chronicle where everything breaks down. If Gehenna is going to happen, then major things like the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla en masse, the Sabbat wiping out entire Paths of Enlightenment, destroying the True Black Hand, Revenant families defecting to the Camarilla, Tremere leaving his body and wiping out all the Tremere anti-tribu in the ritual to do so, etc. are all fine ideas. They give a very strong sense that things are breaking down. In such a world, the Masquerade is going to break down. This is not that much of a problem because human society will start to self-destruct too since Gehenna is just one aspect of the end of the world. The very concept of this chronicle requires the setting to become something unrecognizable. That can be a very intriguing, fascinating, and fun chronicle.<br /> <br /> But if people just want Gehenna to be a looming threat that may or may not happen in the near or distant future, and they want to keep all the toys in the toybox to use again and again, then all of these concepts from Revised are just terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>A guy watches the window shop across the street every day. The shop has two types of decorative windows, one with clear glass panels in the pattern of a Fleur de Lys, or a skull, and a stained glass window with blues, reds, yellows, and greens making a picture out of the book of Revelation, or Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Again and again, he sees customers go in and do the same thing. They buy the stained glass window, then replace every tiny bit of stained glass with a clear piece because &quot;they don't want to deal with the colors.&quot; They want clear glass, but they keep buying the window that only comes in stained glass and replacing each piece, while the clear patterned windows just gather dust right next to them.<br /> <br /> The guy scratches his head as he watches this happen, again and again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-30-2022, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T16:49:40-07:00","id":1488506,"title":"","content":"I sincerely hate him, but not to the point of ignoring his existence. I could see myself using him, although I haven't yet. My main problem with him is that he kind of give the feel of &quot;coming out of nowhere&quot; and making a clan feel kind of powerless (the Tremere). I mean a clan that since the first edition was about vampire wizards and then there's a &quot;guy&quot; that came out of nowhere and make them look silly. It felt a bit like &quot;fan service&quot; and Justin Achilles way of starting the end of the setting (which sucked in my opinion). But as he is, G\u00f6ring and Himmler vampires are surely worse than him lol, but he's one of my least favorite &quot;all-powerful Methuselah&quot; in the setting. Specially because having him breaking the curse, that was theoretically enforced by Tremere himself, felt like &quot;Gary Sue&quot;. He's damn powerful and all, sure, but he doesn't have Blood Sorcery 10.<br /> <br /> In the end, I could see myself using him in a story, he's far from being as well-developed as Mithras, Shaitan, Goratrix, Menele, Helena or Baba Yaga, but could still see some use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T17:13:36-07:00","id":1488507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488503#post1488503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A guy watches the window shop across the street every day. The shop has two types of decorative windows, one with clear glass panels in the pattern of a Fleur de Lys, or a skull, and a stained glass window with blues, reds, yellows, and greens making a picture out of the book of Revelation, or Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Again and again, he sees customers go in and do the same thing. They buy the stained glass window, then replace every tiny bit of stained glass with a clear piece because &quot;they don't want to deal with the colors.&quot; They want clear glass, but they keep buying the window that only comes in stained glass and replacing each piece, while the clear patterned windows just gather dust right next to them.<br /> <br /> The guy scratches his head as he watches this happen, again and again...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t get it, and it frustrates me when I don\u2019t get stuff. Can you please explain?<br /> <br /> I neither love Ur-Shulgi nor hate him. He\u2019s just an NPC to me; he\u2019s just there. I like that he was a child when he was alive, but that\u2019s cause I like the concept of super-powered children/teens. I think he makes a decent villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T22:27:17-07:00","id":1488533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition#post1488463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just curious as he can't be the only misfire that this series created.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there's a lot of interesting considerations about the character from many angles, I'll first take the question asked head-on.<br /> <br /> <b>Yes, there is competition</b>.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi is the most recent big misfire in terms of official NPCs, and his place in the final metaplot really gave him a very prominent position in Post-Judgement discussions, that's why you'll mostly read about him than other big misfires. But they existed, plenty of them.<br /> <br /> Based only on visible community reaction, which is a very problematic method, but the one I have right now, I'd say this dubious honor is actually still solidly in the hands of a dude called <b>Samuel Haight</b>. He started fine, then devolved into a series of gonzo shenanigans with increasing stakes and power moves, but decreasing writing quality to ground it, and generally became the poster child of many of the worse mistakes of 2nd edition, even more than Ur-Shulgi is for the worse of Revised.<br /> <br /> Do not read on this that either edition was bad or anything, just that those characters ended up summarizing their bad sides.<br /> <br /> They're also <i>extremely high profile</i>, which is a very important characteristic for this reaction. Vampire Himler is bad, but just a side-piece in <i>Berlin by Night</i>. That means far less layers know about him and, even if everyone knew, his impact on the setting is minimal, so few people will have strong opinion attached to the character. Both Ur-Shulgi and, for the plots of the time, Haight are central points on huge events, things that are hard to ignore while following the setting's development. Haight's story basically <b>was the metaplot</b> for a time.<br /> <br /> My <b>personal</b> opinion is that Ur-Shulgi is a worse character and with a more harmful impact, and I do hate him more. But that's me. Sam probably gets the prize in the long run and for more players, just because even Ur-Shulgi couldn't be so ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488477#post1488477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Is Ur-Shulgi actually hated or loved to hate?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both. Any one of those for some, both for others, as they're not self-excluding.<br /> <br /> The problem with Ur-Shulgi is two fold. One of those <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> explained very well, the guy is, as you said it, a wrecking ball on the setting. It comes and just breaks half a dozen centuries old aspects of life for no other reason than he can and wants to.<br /> <br /> Yet, what really pisses people off is the second aspect: he's a stupid character. Not as in what he does is bad. What he did would be done anyway. He was a plot device to produce a number of changes to the Banu Haqim that were in the making already, the wrecking ball part was a given in context, whatever your opinion on it is.<br /> <br /> What adds insult to it is simply that Ur-Shulgi is a boring character that comes out of nowhere, shows less personality than a wooden plank, and shows his power with what amounts to him waving his pinky and the setting going boom. Not that it was literally that, but that it was <i><u>litera<b>ri</b>ly</u></i> that. There's no drama, no building tension, no interesting presentation, no nothing.<br /> <br /> So you either buy into the basic premise or you don't. The premise is that with the coming Gehenna, old horrors are awakening and the modern world, including modern Kindred society, is nothing against them. I mean, that's not a bad premise for a game. But it isn't the only one and for each player that enjoys it, there's another that finds it boring at best. And the character adds <b>zero</b> to it. Nothing at all.<br /> <br /> I challenge anyone who likes him (and that's not a problem, be my guest if you do) to point any interesting aspect of the character other than he's a Methuselah that awoke and broke the <i>status quo</i> just because he can. Defending the premise itself doesn't count, it is valid already. Just give anything Ur-Shulgi has to him besides being the trope to the letter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T23:21:17-07:00","id":1488537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488533#post1488533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I challenge anyone who likes him (and that's not a problem, be my guest if you do) to point any interesting aspect of the character other than he's a Methuselah that awoke and broke the <i>status quo</i> just because he can. Defending the premise itself doesn't count, it is valid already. Just give anything Ur-Shulgi has to him besides being the trope to the letter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit to a certain level of appreciation for Ur-Shulgi's anti-religiosity as well as its relationship to the Baali plus the origins of the Banu Haqim. If you remove Ur-Shulgi from the context of being a huge wrecking ball to the setting, there's still some other elements to the character that you can use inside a campaign.<br /> <br /> 1. There's an aggressively idolatrous and cult-like group of Banu Haqim that despise the idea there's any member of their Clan who worships someone other than Haqim the antediluvian. This precludes Islam, Christianity, and other monotheistic believers but also other pre-Islamic deities. It is such an out of context problem but believable when there's an ancient who might be teaching this interpretation. It reminds me a bit of Marius who struggled with the Christian guilt of Anne Rice's later vampires because, well, he predated Christianity.<br /> <br /> 2. Ur-Shulgi possibly being Baali in a way that means that potentially the Sorcerer caste of the Assamites are a Baali bloodline that was &quot;adopted&quot; by Haqim. All of the Sorcerers are descended from Ur-Shulgi but is that because he infiltrated the ranks of the Assamites, was converted to being Baali, or is a Baali who <i>converted to being Banu Haqim</i>? Is it possible Ur-Shulgi sought a form of redemption in the ranks of Haqim and his fanatical loyalty is because he has seen the monsters that vampires like him fight?<br /> <br /> 3. Ur-Shulgi was embraced &quot;when the skies rained blood and the moon was black&quot; or something like that. It's interesting to possibly deal with a vampire who has a completely alien view of time and history who might well hail from an era where reaity was fundamentally different from the way it is taught. Vampires from the Dark Ages can talk about fairies and magic and witches but what about people who come from an era where gods walked among humans and physics may well have been different? Is his memory faulty or does he know a truth forgotten?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T04:14:43-07:00","id":1488552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488503#post1488503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A guy watches the window shop across the street every day. The shop has two types of decorative windows, one with clear glass panels in the pattern of a Fleur de Lys, or a skull, and a stained glass window with blues, reds, yellows, and greens making a picture out of the book of Revelation, or Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Again and again, he sees customers go in and do the same thing. They buy the stained glass window, then replace every tiny bit of stained glass with a clear piece because &quot;they don't want to deal with the colors.&quot; They want clear glass, but they keep buying the window that only comes in stained glass and replacing each piece, while the clear patterned windows just gather dust right next to them.<br /> <br /> The guy scratches his head as he watches this happen, again and again...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's more like hes selling a stained glass and a brick smash pack combo for a good price and the owner gets increasingly annoyed you're not using the brick so he tries increasingly drastic measures structured to try and get you to launch the brick. All the while the customer is scratching his head as to why the storekeeper wants you to smash the window, never realising the window has more value. <br /> <br /> At this stage 20+ years on the only people thinking about using the brick in any context are probably considering inserting it into our hypothetical salesperson as he's still constantly trying to get you to wreck your nice window. To point it might be damaging the quality of the windows.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a side my current current setting meta is gehenna was cancelled when ul-shurgi and/or member of the 3rd got drone striked/vacuum bombed in prelude to the 2nd inquisition .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-31-2022, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T04:18:37-07:00","id":1488553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Ur-Shurgi the most hated in VTM or is there competition? </div> </div> </div>He... she... it is not<br /> That honor goes to <b>Samuel Haight</b>; former Kinfolk, former ghoul, former Skin Dancer, former Mage, currently an ashtray somewhere in the ruins of Stygia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T04:22:55-07:00","id":1488554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488553#post1488553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He... she... it is not<br /> <br /> That honor goes to <b>Samuel Haight</b>; former Kinfolk, former ghoul, former Skin Dancer, former Mage, currently an ashtray somewhere in the ruins of Stygia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to say I don't think Samuel Haight is hated by anyone. He's a silly character but unless you played a group of silly adventures in the back of several books and CHAOS FACTOR, he's not going to be a factor in anyone's game. He's STUPID in his power gaming, which is a shame, because I really like the idea of him being the only Slasher villain in a Gothic Horror game.<br /> <br /> But he's not really going to impact most people's games.<br /> <br /> I also like the Storytelling Vault game SKINNER which inspired me to write THE MURDER OF MODIUS.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/115057/W20-Skinner-SAS\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...20-Skinner-SAS</a><br /> <br /> It is a OPP product so I consider it canon for these forums as well. HAIGHT'S RESURRECTION....as an ordinary Garou who undoubtedly gets murdered by the PCs.<br /> <br /> Sam also gave us the Skin Dancers tribe that are awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T05:19:52-07:00","id":1488556,"title":"","content":"I mean with Samuel the response is &quot;lol no&quot; ur-shurgi you have to write around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T05:23:21-07:00","id":1488557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488556#post1488556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean with Samuel the response is &quot;lol no&quot; ur-shurgi you have to write around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Samuel Haight was also a bad prank on the readers as the developers deliberately made him ridiculous because, apparently, making him an immortal werewolf wasn't cool enough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T06:56:55-07:00","id":1488561,"title":"","content":"I don't overly care about Ur-Shulgi one way or the other. I don't really like him, but Ialso don't hate him. I think he fills his role in the metaplot adequately. <br /> <br /> That said, in general I do like the idea of ancient blood gods (like Ur-Shulgi or Baba Yaga) awakening. Vampires so ancient that decidedly modern concepts like the Masquerade or the Silence of the Blood are foreign concepts. They tend to view those things as a sign of weakness among modern vampires rather than a sign that humanity has grown so powerful in such an incredibly short span of time. Of course any Methuselah is powerful, but for these true Methuselah, the Jyhad is not something to be played while hiding behind masks but rather something to be played in person and so they take a level of personal action that other vampires more familiar with recent trends would never do. <br /> <br /> These ancient blood gods are giants in the swimming pool and where they go, they leave a wake that others can only hope to swim or be doomed to sink. Vampires like Baba Yaga or Ur-Shulgi are used to being worshipped and treated like gods and over the course of many thousands and thousands of years have bought into their own hype. But that hype is mostly accurate. I think that's fairly cool as long as such vampires aren't terribly common, and we've only had a few so far. Baba Yaga was used and treated really poorly, but so far I think what's been done with Ur-Shulgi is adequate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-31-2022, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T07:24:51-07:00","id":1488563,"title":"","content":"I just treat ur-Shulgi as nearing wakefulness, not awake. That's how V20 does it, and it allows you to have him influence things, cause the Schism, and provide a possible sign of the Apocalypse, without him actually being the Apocalypse (yet).<br /> <br /> Once he's awake, then he has to do something or someone has to deal with him. As a liminal being between torpor and the waking world, he gets to be a plot hook while keeping things vague.<br /> <br /> Then again, Caine may be running round as a taxi driver, and Tremere and Saulot are certainly both active, so maybe having ur-Shulgi awaken isn't the end of the world (pun half-intended).<br /> <br /> ETA: OOC, Sam Haight seems the most hated generally, followed by Huitzilopochtli (from the same book).<br /> <br /> IC, I think most other VTM characters hate Nergal (if they know of him), or the Baali in general (if they don't). The Baali are the most reviled vampires in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-31-2022, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T07:35:38-07:00","id":1488564,"title":"","content":"I hate metaplot. But, IRL, there are plenty of unexpected twists and turns. A country-ending fleet gets destroyed in a storm, at the end of a grand campaign the great leader gets killed by cancer or a stray bullet. Men make plans; god laughs. An ancient waking up and upending one of the minor sects isn't exactly out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T08:29:08-07:00","id":1488568,"title":"","content":"Please someone delete this mistake, I'm still working on the post...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-31-2022, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T08:29:08-07:00","id":1488569,"title":"","content":"Coming soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T09:45:20-07:00","id":1488575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488537#post1488537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit to a certain level of appreciation for Ur-Shulgi's anti-religiosity as well as its relationship to the Baali plus the origins of the Banu Haqim. If you remove Ur-Shulgi from the context of being a huge wrecking ball to the setting, there's still some other elements to the character that you can use inside a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair observations, I'll add my opinions on them. That doesn't make them less of a fair answer to my challenge, necessarily, at least not the number 2.<br /> <br /> 1 - The aggressive cult of Haqim is good and makes sense, but it is so because of the Web of Knives, not because of Ur-Shulgi. While he was made responsible for the Purge in Revised, that is just an aspect of his Wrecking Ball facet. Other than that, a number of clan members becoming completely indoctrinated into this idolatry just because this old dude says so is, imo, plainly stupid. And if they didn't need the old dude to start to think like that, then the old dude isn't a relevant factor. His own motivation only demonstrates his mental ineptitude, because his idolatry come completely from personal childish emotions and this is demonstrated by the fact that there are others who personally knew Haqim and they can attest that Ur-Shulgi is making shit up.<br /> <br /> So much so is this that V20 kept this plot while removing Ur-Shulgi from it and it works perfectly fine. If you find it better or worse is irrelevant to the fact that it works without him, no problems.<br /> <br /> 2 - A good one, although not a canonical one. The text linking him to the Baali is good, but is <i>Word of God</i> instead of official material, so there's an innate caveat to it and anything that derives from it. Even then, I would say it makes his story better, but doesn't change his personality (or lack thereof) too much.<br /> <br /> 3 - Sorry, but this is just an aspect of the trope, his being so old and powerful that stories of his first days exist only as epic myths that may or may not be true at face value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488554#post1488554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to say I don't think Samuel Haight is hated by anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but he definitely is.<br /> <br /> If you think this is deserved or necessary is another matter, and I do agree that the hate against him is overblown. But Haight was hated with a vengeance by many, many players back then. and by some still. The degree of this hate have never been properly measured and probably never will, each person has only their own observations and natural bias to form an opinion on it, but it was definitely a thing.<br /> <br /> Haight deserving any hate is a matter of opinion, but his getting it is an observable, well documented fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488561#post1488561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, in general I do like the idea of ancient blood gods (like Ur-Shulgi or Baba Yaga) awakening. Vampires so ancient that decidedly modern concepts like the Masquerade or the Silence of the Blood are foreign concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said the trope itself is fair, despite not my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> But other characters do follow this concept and they generally have more about them than Ur-Shulgi. Helena and Menele, Baba Yaga, Mithras, while not exceedingly common they're still a few running around and they have more to their personality, motivations and actions than Ur-Shulgi. That's why I say he's a very bare-bones use of the trope. Even Baba Yaga, despite coming in a very bad book, has a more complex and interesting personality, plans and behavior, and she is just as much an impossibly ancient sorceress.<br /> <br /> Other than that, though, I must explain why I don't like this trope so much. First, the game always assumed as a premise that those are still hidden monsters that like to manipulate from the shadows instead of taking things in their own hands. It is just that their motivation is different, instead of fearing humanity, they fear giving too much info about themselves to their equally ancient and powerful rivals. All the other Methuselah play the part, Ur-Shulgi as the sole exception seems just stupid instead of alien and powerful.<br /> <br /> Second, it is as much a part of the setting that there are things above anyone's individual power, including what humans can do as a society. And I like this, because I much prefer the idea that context and the World\u2122 is, in the end, stronger than any individual. That's even codified in the Traditions, whose interpretations and force changed through time, but none even among the oldest Methuselah claim to not be there since forever and generally good advice. Being at open war with your food is a lose-lose situation.<br /> <br /> And special mention must be made to the idea of loosing touch with times is as much a liability as being unaware of ancient powers. What makes the most powerful and influential really old Methuselah, well, powerful and influential, is that they took their sweet time to update themselves about the state of the world, sometimes during their slumber.<br /> <br /> For Ur-Shulgi, I think a completely reasonable consequence for his actions would be for other Methuselah to set things in motion to override just the specific protections of Alamut that would prevent such a thing and have the place nuked. Not just because I don't like him, but because that would be a much needed reminder of why vampires hide and the cost of being careless just because you are powerful. Equally powerful monsters that are moving around with a lower profile would just shake their heads with the fate of Haqim's boy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: it is sad to know that a far better character could have been made if they just used the bulk of information we actually have in the Real Life <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shulgi\" target=\"_blank\">Shulgi, King of Ur</a> from whom his name was taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-31-2022, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:15:34-07:00","id":1488583,"title":"","content":"This Samuel Haight sounds incredibly absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:39:45-07:00","id":1488587,"title":"","content":"One of the easiest ways to circumvent up shurgi is just to nerf it. Maybe only have one or two disciplines are 9 and have part of his power being political, maybe his presence simply swings things in favour of the Web of knives causing the political shitshow. <br /> <br /> The other idea I had is haquim actually wants his clan in all the sects so the little goblin could simple is his big boy piece in some 4d jyhad chess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-31-2022, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T12:41:35-07:00","id":1488594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488583#post1488583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Samuel Haight sounds incredibly absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sam Haight? <i>Absurd</i>? I can't imagine why anyone would think this at all. It's not like he was described in a one page ad as <a href=\"https://twitter.com/bauthorfowler/status/1553834108144340992\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;The Ultimate Badass,&quot;</a> or anything... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T13:28:06-07:00","id":1488596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488583#post1488583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Samuel Haight sounds incredibly absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude was made to basically be the &quot;half everything&quot;. A Kinfolk that developed the Rite that creates the Skin Dancers (so he became a Werewolf without having all the disadvantages of a Werewolf all the time), then he forced a lot of spirits to teach him Gifts (so he has more of those than expected for Ronin), then he became a Ghoul of a low gen vampire and started to be a vampire hunter for the Blood and Disciplines (which he learned faster than normal because), and as a powerful hunter with all the abilities of a Werewolf at his disposal, Blood wasn't much of a problem. Then he stole Wonders from several Mages and killed an Archmage for one that gave him the abilities of a Mage with Arete 7 and a lot of Spheres.<br /> <br /> The further you go in his story, the less time is spent with setting up the story or explaining things and the more the sources of power are just there. The Skin Dancers are really neat and work really well by themselves. Wonders with the capacity to give a Sleeper the full abilities of a Mage at any Arete rating simply do not exist, there's no justification of how or why even an Archmage had one of those and he killed the Mage and stole the loot behind the scenes so the author didn't had to even try to explain how the hell that happened.<br /> <br /> Plans are said to have existed to have him similarly emulate/steal/absorb the powers of upcoming slats, maybe become a permanent fixture of the whole WoD, when they decided to simply have him killed, IIRC in <i>Chaos Factor</i>, a module completely centered on him and crossover-oriented (obviously), after many appearances where his arrival in a city was worse news than a tripple invasion by Baali, the Sabbat and a Garou Sept while an Ante is awakening.<br /> <br /> For a time there was a rumor that this would result in him coming back as a Wraith that somehow retained every other power he had, but then <i>Revised</i> rolled over and expunged any intention to do over-the-top crossover gonzo in anything near that level again. The next official news we had was that while he did became a Wraith, he was soulforged into an ashtray, later used as a joke reference in an image of the aftermath of the Sixth Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488587#post1488587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the easiest ways to circumvent up shurgi is just to nerf it. Maybe only have one or two disciplines are 9 and have part of his power being political, maybe his presence simply swings things in favour of the Web of knives causing the political shitshow.<br /> <br /> The other idea I had is haquim actually wants his clan in all the sects so the little goblin could simple is his big boy piece in some 4d jyhad chess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Circumventing or improving Ur-Shulgi is easy, which is more evidence to how bare-bones he is, but certainly a benefit that Haight couldn't enjoy so easily.<br /> <br /> I think just changing the focus to the actual clan instead of making things his sole doing is a big start without any need to mess with his purposefully-non-existent sheet. <i>Lore of the Clans</i> basically did that, and it is pretty good at that. With this, his presence could very well be the tipping point for the changes instead of the sole cause of it all.<br /> <br /> The Web of Knives being the extremists all along is a given, and his coming back would justify the WoK finally deciding to take actions they have been wanting to for a long time. Their building up of power comes from a long time, but they still couldn't rule the whole clan and fill all the needed roles by themselves. More than any particular big power, he is a Sorcerer that could reign in the caste within the WoK's line of thought, by force if necessary, and then finally make the Viziers disposable from their PoV.<br /> <br /> Key elements here are at the hands of the Sorcerers: the Tremere Curse and the rite <b><i>From Marduk's Throat</i></b>. Together those two mean the WoK couldn't just ditch Al-Ashrad and his Sorcerers, as they held the only hope of revoking the Tremere Curse and the only tool for the realization of the <b>Path of Blood</b> under the curse.<br /> <br /> My personal change to even V20 would be that the Sorcerers probably found the answer to the Tremere Curse long ago, they're just not using it. At least Al-Ashrad has, but probably some other Sorcerers do, too. And why would they? The Tremere Curse put a lid on the Baali Curse that was spreading like a virus and was obviously more problematic, as any sane person could see from a mile, and getting rid of it would just free the WoK to be a bigger problem. From the perspective of moderates within, the WoK was obviously the biggest threat to the Banu Haqim, both as a clan and for their mission, at the present and almost since their appearance, a threat only getting worse by the day. Ur-Shulgi then could end the Curse so quickly because he could piece the correct ritual from his access to what the Sorcerers already have, and probably guess that they've been deceiving the &quot;loyalists&quot; about it.<br /> <br /> Still I would have him literally nuked after a time. Again, not because I hate him (which I do), but because I think the idea of one of those monsters being nuked to up the ante is a good addition whether you want to go full Gehenna or not (it ups the Ante of what breaking the Masquerade means while the world makes it harder and harder to keep). By the way, this could be one of the plans the Schismatics form within the Camarilla, cementing the power of the sect as being above all derived from its presence within institutions rather than the sheer power of its elders (and Methuselah).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T14:58:01-07:00","id":1488600,"title":"","content":"The more I hear about this Haight character described. The more I wonder if you are having some fun with the comparative newbie like me as this sounds like something that a child would create or something out of Palladium Books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T14:58:56-07:00","id":1488601,"title":"","content":"But I think you are not exaggerating at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T15:54:44-07:00","id":1488610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488601#post1488601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think you are not exaggerating at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haight is actually the subject of a practical joke in that the developers kept making him more and more ridiculous to see if the editors would slap them down.<br /> <br /> They didn't.<br /> <br /> So he went from being an immortal hedge mage Garou ghoul to a True Magic with a magic sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-31-2022, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:14:54-07:00","id":1488612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488610#post1488610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haight is actually the subject of a practical joke in that the developers kept making him more and more ridiculous to see if the editors would slap them down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't know about that. You keep bringing up that he was a practical joke, but I personally don't know the sources or anything, but in the sense that I literally don't know. It does make some sense because he's really out there.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> I understand the feeling. Unfortunately he graced some otherwise good and really influential supplements before everyone coming together to kill him, so it is less of a joke and more of a crime, but not by me.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Answering your question, no Ur-Shulgi is <b>not</b> the most hated character in VtM, probably. That would be a happier world to live in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:15:10-07:00","id":1488613,"title":"","content":"To be very honest, a part of me kinda likes Haight lol. I mean he had the potential to be a good antagonist, but the stories went downhill after a certain point. In the end, I still think he's better than Ur-Shulgi as, at least, he doesn't affect the whole metaplot as Ur-Shulgi. A ST could easily ignore him, of course one might say that the same could be said about Ur-Shilgi, but it's much harder to &quot;ignore Ur-Shulgi&quot;, his actions affected the whole setting, etc. That's why I consider Haight just a somewhat &quot;funny&quot; character concept, he's not shoved down our throats the way Ur-Shulgi is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:52:20-07:00","id":1488617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488613#post1488613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be very honest, a part of me kinda likes Haight lol. I mean he had the potential to be a good antagonist, but the stories went downhill after a certain point. In the end, I still think he's better than Ur-Shulgi as, at least, he doesn't affect the whole metaplot as Ur-Shulgi. A ST could easily ignore him, of course one might say that the same could be said about Ur-Shilgi, but it's much harder to &quot;ignore Ur-Shulgi&quot;, his actions affected the whole setting, etc. That's why I consider Haight just a somewhat &quot;funny&quot; character concept, he's not shoved down our throats the way Ur-Shulgi is.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're both less offensive now than they were back them (well, Lysander may need some time to digest Haight right now), to be honest. The setting grew, the world went on, the context changed and the people that read those things when they were new grew too. As concepts and tools they're ok, can be better used and have been. Advantages when you have an RPG instead of a common novel or other fiction, where you have to sell the character within the story instead of as a free-for-use story element.<br /> <br /> But yeah. I do generally agree that this is what makes Ur-Shulgi more harmful to the setting and a worse offender. He's boring, but the kind of boring you're &quot;not allowed&quot; to ignore. And while the changes would happen anyway, he does shape then, so the consequences go far beyond him even if you're not interested in him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:57:23-07:00","id":1488618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488612#post1488612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't know about that. You keep bringing up that he was a practical joke, but I personally don't know the sources or anything, but in the sense that I literally don't know. It does make some sense because he's really out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one of Phil Brucato's interviews with the Gentleman Gamer, he talked a bit about the history of Sam Haight. If I recall, he said that Haight was kind of an office joke. He might have started out as a serious antagonist (kind of like how he appears in the W20 SAS), but I think he amused the writers.<br /> <br /> Here's a decent history of Samuel Haight: <a href=\"https://boardgamegeek.com/geeklist/147814/history-samuel-haight-spoilers\" target=\"_blank\">https://boardgamegeek.com/geeklist/1...aight-spoilers</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T17:06:25-07:00","id":1488619,"title":"","content":"Turning a character with an interesting concept into the 90s equivalent of Guild Wars 2's <a href=\"https://www.engadget.com/2013-12-10-flameseeker-chronicles-the-trouble-with-scarlet-in-guild-wars-2.html\" target=\"_blank\">Scarlet Briar</a> is a heck of a joke.<br /> <br /> Doesn't look like the audience was laughing much back then, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T17:10:15-07:00","id":1488622,"title":"","content":"I may have to do an homage to Samuel Haight in my next PSYCHO KILLERS IN LOVE book. &quot;The werewolf vampire serial killer of other werewolf vampires. Oh and he knows magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T17:23:45-07:00","id":1488624,"title":"","content":"One of my main gripes with some people who criticize Haight (beyond the fact that I love to play the &quot;Devil's Advocate&quot; lol) is that some of the criticism he got from some people I knew, imply that a &quot;recurring villain&quot; is somehow a bad thing for the setting and I'm of the complete opposite idea. Good antagonists are what makes stories good to begin with, if you have a good antagonist you have half (or perhaps more) of what you need to make the story good. When I was a kid, Goratrix was my favorite character from the setting. I mean he's charming, ambitious, genius wizard that invented many things and then betrayed the clan, etc. He was the kind of villain I thought could make many interesting stories, of course of a different scale, as he's not the kind of villain the group is likely to beat in a &quot;fist fight&quot;, but then the same could be said about Baba Yaga or even Vecna if we talk about other game lines as well.<br /> <br /> So, to sum up, when I was a kid I really wanted to have this kind of antagonists created for the setting, but then I rarely had, Goratrix for instance, was never fully explored to make him a great villain where the PCs are going to try to stop him from doing something (and the only story where you can deal with him, i.e. the Transylvania Chronicles, the PCs can't even deal with him properly and are basically witness to the major plot happening), unless the ST creates everything himself, say he creates a story where Goratrix is going to do something nasty and the PCs need to do something, even if it's just to gather allies to deal with him, etc, and that is exactly where I want to get. One of the problems I've always seen in the WoD is that it takes a huge deal of effort for ST, because they need to create many things themselves and many times from scratch, by the way I have mentioned in a thread some time ago that I have a friend who is a ST for some decades and he gave up ST Vampire exactly because he said it's just &quot;too much work&quot;, the setting doesn't give us many tools and creating a city and a story, etc, from scratch is a huge deal of work. I mean, I really love this kind of work, because I love writing and creating, but sometimes I wish we had more fully explored antagonists etc. and a some &quot;help to my worldbuilding&quot; and that's why my tendency is to always kind of &quot;welcome&quot; the likes of Haight, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T18:43:21-07:00","id":1488636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488624#post1488624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good antagonists are what makes stories good to begin with, if you have a good antagonist you have half (or perhaps more) of what you need to make the story good. When I was a kid, Goratrix was my favorite character from the setting. I mean he's charming, ambitious, genius wizard that invented many things and then betrayed the clan, etc. He was the kind of villain I thought could make many interesting stories, of course of a different scale, as he's not the kind of villain the group is likely to beat in a &quot;fist fight&quot;, but then the same could be said about Baba Yaga or even Vecna if we talk about other game lines as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all great, except &quot;Sammy, the Ultimate Badass,&quot; only <i>started</i> out as a good antagonist. Then instead of keeping him in his lane, they tried to make him the Tharizdun of the WoD.<br /> <br /> No one's saying he couldn't, or shouldn't have appeared in Vampire or Mage Chronicles. Someone nutty enough to hunt Werewolves <i>and</i> tough enough to survive would make, say, a <i>great</i> assassin against a Gangrel, or the <i>perfect</i> person to explore ancient ruins for Magical artifacts (assuming either such things exist in Ascension). But, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> pointed out, they tried to make him &quot;half of everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the World of Darkness <i>did</i> need an &quot;ultimate&quot; antagonist for all of the lines, and it's debatable whether or not they did, they should have used, in my opinion, <b>Pentex</b>. Sam Haight is just one guy (and in a way, so is Ur- Shulgi), but Pentex is a world-spanning organization, with tentacles everywhere. Their board of directors had both Malkavian antitribu <i>and</i> Giovanni. Frankly, they shouldn't have been able to restrict themselves to Werewolf antagonists if they <i>tried</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>So</i>, instead of Pentex being <i>just</i> a tool of the Wyrm, Pentex could have been a whole thing entirely, testing new toys for the Technocracy against &quot;reality deviants,&quot; or helping Sabbat wage their wars against the Camarilla. Imagine, sometime around the Industrial Revolution, Sabbat (or Baali) Vampires, Technocratic (or Nephandi or Marauder) Magi, and the most cunning Black Spiral Dancer Werewolves (or Metis or just Kinfolk) pooling resources or helping each other double team their rivals. Maybe they're all contacted by a Wraith (or one of the &quot;bad guys&quot; in Changeling). Like Big Boy Caprice in the Dick Tracy movie, this contact invites antagonist characters from each book, sells them on the benefits of working together, whacks the one guy who's &quot;not interested&quot; in some spectacular fashion, and boom; you have the first board of directors for Pentex. Only this would be a Pentex that truly spans the <i>entire</i> &quot;World of Darkness.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-31-2022, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:13:49-07:00","id":1488638,"title":"","content":"I think a major reason why Samuel Haight was disliked is that since the key concepts about him are unique to him, the only way he could have continued to be used as an antagonist is to give him plot armor to prevent the PCs from killing him. If he got killed, an ST just couldn't replace him with yet another Skindancer Ghoul Mage with Thaumaturgy. There's only so many of them that could exist, right? So the sourcebooks he appeared in gave all sorts of bad instructions to the ST that were bound to piss off players to no end.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Haight has escaped... The storyteller can use Haight as a continuing nemesis in future stories...&quot;</i> - Valkenburg Foundation<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Haight can reappear as the Storyteller likes, but the characters should not have the opportunity to kill him. He will be appearing in future White Wolf products.&quot;</i> - Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Pursuit of Sam Haight will prove futile, under no circumstances should Haight be captured, as he will be showing up again in future supplements.&quot;</i> - Book of Chantries<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;There is absolutely no chance that the pack could locate him, even if they tried.&quot;</i> - Rage Across the Amazon<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's fun for the PCs. This is classic White Wolf railroading at its worst. (This was a big problem for LOTS of RPGs around this time.)<br /> <br /> The original concept of Sam Haight is perfectly fine. The creator or reviver of the Skindancers. A brand new enemy for the Garou has been created. He could very well be a classic, fun repeating villain in any Werewolf chronicle. Or if he is killed, since the secret is now out there, he could easily be replaced by one of his disciples who in turn might become a classic, fun repeating villain of his own.<br /> <br /> Now if you use a faction, as opposed to a specific individual, to initiate the game plot, then there's no problem to keep it going despite whom the PCs might defeat or destroy. In literature, there is no problem with Dracula being the antagonist for the entire book. In RPG games, it's important to have a fall back plan in case the PC Johnathon Harker kills Dracula in Transylvania. The ST needs to be flexible enough to go, &quot;You know what, that's fine. Dracula's destroyed. I'll just send the Brides of Dracula out for revenge to London after Harker returns there. I can preserve most of what I planned anyway using them. They Brides will be the real villains!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:28:01-07:00","id":1488640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488636#post1488636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all great, except &quot;Sammy, the Ultimate Badass,&quot; only <i>started</i> out as a good antagonist. Then instead of keeping him in his lane, they tried to make him the Tharizdun of the WoD.<br /> <br /> No one's saying he couldn't, or shouldn't have appeared in Vampire or Mage Chronicles. Someone nutty enough to hunt Werewolves <i>and</i> tough enough to survive would make, say, a <i>great</i> assassin against a Gangrel, or the <i>perfect</i> person to explore ancient ruins for Magical artifacts (assuming either such things exist in Ascension). But, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> pointed out, they tried to make him &quot;half of everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the World of Darkness <i>did</i> need an &quot;ultimate&quot; antagonist for all of the lines, and it's debatable whether or not they did, they should have used, in my opinion, <b>Pentex</b>. Sam Haight is just one guy (and in a way, so is Ur- Shulgi), but Pentex is a world-spanning organization, with tentacles everywhere. Their board of directors had both Malkavian antitribu <i>and</i> Giovanni. Frankly, they shouldn't have been able to restrict themselves to Werewolf antagonists if they <i>tried</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>So</i>, instead of Pentex being <i>just</i> a tool of the Wyrm, Pentex could have been a whole thing entirely, testing new toys for the Technocracy against &quot;reality deviants,&quot; or helping Sabbat wage their wars against the Camarilla. Imagine, sometime around the Industrial Revolution, Sabbat (or Baali) Vampires, Technocratic (or Nephandi or Marauder) Magi, and the most cunning Black Spiral Dancer Werewolves (or Metis or just Kinfolk) pooling resources or helping each other double team their rivals. Maybe they're all contacted by a Wraith (or one of whatever the &quot;bad guys&quot; in Changeling are). Like Big Boy Caprice in the Dick Tracy movie, this contact invites antagonist characters from each book, sells them on the benefits of working together, whacks the one guy who's &quot;not interested&quot; in some spectacular fashion, and boom; you have the first board of directors for Pentex. Only this would be a Pentex that truly spans the <i>entire</i> &quot;World of Darkness.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I agree that Samuel Haight lost track and became a bad antagonist (in any case, I think he's FAR from being anything remotely close to Tharizdun lol), so to speak, but his role could have been made interesting. Also, although I understand the appeal Pentex has for some people, in my opinion their appeal is applied to a very specific kind of story. Besides, there's the fact that it's an organization, it doesn't have the same appeal as a personified antagonist. For this kind of role of organization to be an &quot;ultimate&quot; antagonist, I'd say the Tal'Mahe'Ra makes a much better job. They have basically every kind of creature and abominations (literally) in their ranks and the organization is very interesting for its darker themes and well-developed history.<br /> All in all, I like the ideal of antagonists for the entire line of games, this could have helped &quot;unify&quot; the setting more, because many times it seems each splat exists in a separate world. So, more stories involving all the different splats would probably help solving this problem. Baba Yaga was a very interesting such character in Rage across Russia, it's a pity the setting gave her a very uninspired ending in a later supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 07-31-2022, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:56:53-07:00","id":1488645,"title":"","content":"@Monteparnas<br /> <br /> &gt;Samuel Haight <br /> Hahahahhahahahahahahahahaha The Power Gamer's Dark Reflection","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T20:18:36-07:00","id":1488647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488640#post1488640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baba Yaga was a very interesting such character in Rage across Russia, it's a pity the setting gave her a very uninspired ending in a later supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>To Grandmother's House really should have been a Werewolf adventure and involved the PC's helping to lead the shapeshifters and other supernatural creatures of Russia in murdering the hell out of her and her Zmei. She was introduced in a Werewolf book, set up as a werewolf antagonist, and then got &quot;worfed&quot; in a vampire book (getting one-shot by another vampire) leaving her entire arc very unfulfilling from any gameline perspective. That's further magnified by the fact that she was the mother of Clan Nosferatu as, apparently she was the only one of Absimiliard's children to never be bloodbound and to have children of her own, so all of the vampires of the Nosferatu clan are descended from her. She was completely mishandled in so many ways from the beginning to the end when you consider her importance to, not just the VtM setting but to the entire World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Hell, even as silly as Sam Haight ended up being, I think he had a better character arc and satisfactory conclusion to his storyline within the metaplot than Baba Yaga did. So far I feel like the gameline has been dealing with, and treating, Ur-Shulgi better than it did with Baba Yaga and hopefully he isn't unceremoniously one-shot by some other supernatural critter in order to build hype for something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-31-2022, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T20:30:22-07:00","id":1488649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488645#post1488645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Samuel Haight<br /> Hahahahhahahahahahahahahaha The Power Gamer's Dark Reflection</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically about it. At the time Sam was being written there was a real push in the WoD community (at least online) from players about mix-and-matching different splat aspects together. And lots of jokes about playing werewolf-vampires with hedge magic and finding ways to stick cybernetic devices from MtA on them, or how to get access to Changeling powers. etc. Samuel Haight was very much intended to be a meta-commentary from the game writers about the community at the time. And more serious players (who hated that sort of &quot;munchkinism&quot;) hated Sam Haight. Players who wanted to powergame looked at him as an inspiration (which just pissed off the serious players even more). And other players just sort of enjoyed the meta-narrative of seeing the writers acknowledge the short of bullshit that some players in the community were trying to do.<br /> <br /> By the time Chaos Factor hit Sam was absolutely intended to be a meta-joke about various gonzo concepts in the WoD fan community as well as about certain players who tried to lean into that too hard. Ultimately Sam was a character where either people hated him and hated the meta-joke he represented, or they hated him while enjoying the meta-joke. At the end I don't think there were too many people who liked him, though in his earliest iteration as the Skin Dancer I think he was pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T20:51:17-07:00","id":1488654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> o Grandmother's House really should have been a Werewolf adventure and involved the PC's helping to lead the shapeshifters and other supernatural creatures of Russia in murdering the hell out of her and her Zmei. She was introduced in a Werewolf book, set up as a werewolf antagonist, and then got &quot;worfed&quot; in a vampire book (getting one-shot by another vampire) leaving her entire arc very unfulfilling from any gameline perspective. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. that story was one of the worst I've read in any supplement. The PCs are basically witness to basically what amounts to be a plot involving getting rid of Baba Yaga, there's almost no player agency in the story, even Giovanni Chronicles and Transylvania Chronicles gave the PCs more agency. In my opinion, it ended up being one of the worst opportunities to make a very interesting inter-splat story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's basically about it. At the time Sam was being written there was a real push in the WoD community (at least online) from players about mix-and-matching different splat aspects together. And lots of jokes about playing werewolf-vampires with hedge magic and finding ways to stick cybernetic devices from MtA on them, etc. Samuel Haight was very much intended to be a meta-commentary from the game writers about the community at the time. And more serious players (who hated that sort of &quot;munchkinism&quot;) hated Sam Haight. Players who wanted to powergame looked at him as an inspiration (which just pissed off the serious players even more). And other players just sort of enjoyed the meta-narrative of seeing the writers acknowledge the short of bullshit that some players in the community were trying to do. </div> </div> </div>Funny thing is that if you want me to be sincere, I've known a deal more of players who really loved Saumel Haight than players who hated him. More than one group of players have approached me asking me to include him in my games lol. I really don't give a damn about &quot;mix and matching&quot;, I don't see an inherent problem in Haight having True Magick disciplines and Gifts, nor about abominations and/or vampires being able to use mage's avatars to perform true Magick in the Guide to Tal'Mahe'Ra. I really don't see any problem with that, they're just different kind of powers. All that matters to me is the quality of the story and in that sense, Samuel Haight's story got really bad after his first appearance and can't help but feel that Ur-Shulgi came out of nowhere as a &quot;Mary Sue&quot; to implement the changes the developers wanted to implement in the games. He's really not convincing enough to me as a character, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, he's <b>boring </b>and it's one of the worst things one can be in any story. I really hoped they went in another direction with Baba Yaga as she really deserved better. Nowadays I don't see many characters that could be made to involve all the splats in a story, perhaps they're going to come up with something, but, to be honest, I think it's very unlikely, what is a shame.<br /> <br /> I don't even remember what happened to the Zmei in <i>To Grandmother's House</i>, I think they were completely ignored, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 08-01-2022, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:08:10-07:00","id":1488655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488654#post1488654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even remember what happened to the Zmei in <i>To Grandmother's House</i>, I think they were completely ignored, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Zmei were just kind of ignored. One of them was officially killed in the past. Several others are still locked away and several others were freed as of Rage Across Russia. But what happened to them is never discussed in To Grandmother's House and I don't believe they've ever been mentioned again in any other books. Considering they were strong enough that the 7 of them and Baba Yaga were able to fight equally against Absimiliard, I always thought they were kind of a big thing to be left unaccounted for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:54:43-07:00","id":1488661,"title":"","content":"<b>Goluko\u200b</b> is a maddened Zmei of Russia that can breathe balefire. He has become radioactive over the years, to the point that he even glows in the dark. In ancient times, he was hunted down and bound by the Silver Fangs in the Taymyr Peninsula, but in time they neglected his resting place and eventually the area was used as a site for thermonuclear testings. Although the detonations could not shatter the magical bonds that held Goluko, radiation slowly devoured his weakened body. He is a 30 feet long dragon body in addition to his 15 foot tail. His once lustrous scales are now sickly green and some are falling off. He has mutated warts growing across his belly as a sign of radiation disease. Rage and pain define his behavior. In the '90s, a group of Black Spiral Dancers has found his resting place and are trying awaken him. If Goluko escapes, the destruction could be on an unprecedented scale. Even Baba Yaga herself would not allow that. But since she is not around anymore...? Bad News<br /> <b>Gregornous Deathwing</b> is one of the seven Zmei of Russia. Anyone who hears his hex scream risks being cursed with calamity. Of all the Great Zmei, Gregornous is the most eager to please the Hag. He believes he only exists to serve the Little Grandmother, and that this is also true to the other Zmei, even if they will not admit it. Therefore, it's only natural that he is inclined to show them how to properly respect their master. His hex scream makes plants wilt, the earth shake, buildings tumble and the life force of the world scream in pain. He was accidentally awakened in a battle between a Technomancer and a Celestial Chorus mage during World War II. The Paradox spirit unleashed during battle purged the area of magick that did not conform to the laws of science, including the binding spell that held the Great Zmei. Always clever, Gregornous laid low, hiding in the wilderness to figure out what was going on in the world since he fell asleep. During this time he secretly watched over Baba Yaga's resting place until she finally rose. After the Hag is gone? Safe to say he want REVENGE!<br /> <b>Illyana</b> is one of the seven Zmei of Russia. With a single word she can make all things within 20 yards of her burst into flames. She lives to collect stories about the exploits of her brothers and has been known to seek the company of her peers. It is said that Illyana alone has the prerogative to visit any of them without invitation (although she does not like Trevero very much). Her greatest passion is the tales of great battles and great deceptions. Illyana knows the true record of the fight with the Antediluvian vampire, and she believes she has a hint on the location of his resting place, but keeps this knowledge a secret, as personal advantage. If someone asks about her race, she will gladly tell them. No matter if they take the knowledge to the grave, at least they will know to the honor of dying to one of the Great Zmei. In this regard she is quiet but deadly. After the Hag died, I think she continnues what she already was doing<br /> <b>\u200bRustarin </b>is the leader of the seven Zmei of Russia. Her commanding gaze can cause a victim to freeze while under her stare. Rustarin still sleeps, although the binding is weak. Her localization is somewhere in Kazakhstan, near the Aral Sea.<br /> <b>Sharkala the Cruel</b> \u200b was a powerful Zmei of Russia. He was destroyed in 1240.<br /> <b>\u200bShazear</b> \u200bis one of the seven Zmei from Russia. He is able to shapeshift and assume human form. Shazear escaped the werewolves hunt completely because they didn't even know that he existed. Shazear has come to love the ways of the &quot;little people&quot;. Of all Zmei he is the most likely to be turned from the path of the Wyrm and back to the path of the Wyld. Due to his long sabbatical amongst humans, he is no longer susceptible to Rustarin's commands through her stare. Gregornous found him after Baba Yaga awakened form her torpor, but Shazear has convinced him that he has only been awake for a few years. If the other Zmei were to know that he wandered for so long without trying to free them, he might not survive their anger. Baba Yaga, though, is the only being that he truly fears. He serves her, but he wants out (and this isn't for ethical reasons, he just can't stand leashes anymore). Now she is gone, he is FREE, so... maybe mingle with the humans<br /> <b>\u200bTrevero</b>\u200b is the strongest of his kind in sheer physical power. Filled with anger and hunger for destruction, he is a servant of the Beast-of-War. He remembers bearing the Maeljin known as Hellbringer on his back in a war against the Garou in the distant past. He carries this memory and a hatred for the werewolves to this day. On June 8, 1908, he broke free from the Rite of Draconic Binding, and the following battle with Uktena, Silver Fangs, and a mage resulted in what became known as the Tunguska event. He was defeated, and the Rite of Draconic Binding was enacted again, sealing him into a deep sleep that not even Baba Yaga can break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T22:08:31-07:00","id":1488664,"title":"","content":"The rise of Ur-Shulgi and the fate of Baba Yaga both demonstrate a developer disinterest in epic level play, and it causes me more disappointment than hate. There's just this line on the scale past which players aren't supposed to have characters, and NPC's aren't to be fought, unless it's by a company-owned character in a novel. The players in Transylvania Chronicle are methusalehs by the final chapter, but there's still a Kuei-Jin guest star NPC who can and likely will thwart Absimiliard's evil scheme for them. Only Lucinda and Fatima could have beaten Mon\u00e7ada, because only they have the necessary plot armor. Maybe this is just what metaplot is, but it feels like the Forgotten Realms. Why be an adventurer when Elminster's adventures are the ones that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T22:22:19-07:00","id":1488666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488664#post1488664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it feels like the Forgotten Realms. Why be an adventurer when Elminster's adventures are the ones that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the premise of Doomed Forgotten Realms. It's basically a &quot;what if&quot; book detailing what would happen if the PCs ended up dying and failing to successfully deal with the threats from the various adventure paths. So the Demon Lords have taken over the Underdark and begun reshaping it into a new Abyss. Baldur's Gate has fallen into Hell. The Elemental Lords have sundered much of the surface, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T22:50:34-07:00","id":1488667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488664#post1488664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rise of Ur-Shulgi and the fate of Baba Yaga both demonstrate a developer disinterest in epic level play, and it causes me more disappointment than hate. There's just this line on the scale past which players aren't supposed to have characters, and NPC's aren't to be fought, unless it's by a company-owned character in a novel. The players in Transylvania Chronicle are methusalehs by the final chapter, but there's still a Kuei-Jin guest star NPC who can and likely will thwart Absimiliard's evil scheme for them. Only Lucinda and Fatima could have beaten Mon\u00e7ada, because only they have the necessary plot armor. Maybe this is just what metaplot is, but it feels like the Forgotten Realms. <b>Why be an adventurer when Elminster's adventures are the ones that matter.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This unfortunately led to the creation of the fucking Shade. Because the idea was to put a dozen Epic Level Archmages worshiping Shar for every Chosen.<br /> <br /> And that just made me wonder why the world wasn't conquered already.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T23:15:26-07:00","id":1488670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488654#post1488654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even remember what happened to the Zmei in <i>To Grandmother's House</i>, I think they were completely ignored, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were ignored because at that point in time the Revised developers had segregated each game line in their own silos. Crossover was now a dirty word. Vampire didn't care at all what would impact the Werewolf game. It only cared about that Baba Yaga was a vampire and thus owned by Vampire. That &quot;story&quot; in Nights of Prophecy was meant as an FU to Werewolf and announce that any crossover was over. If I remember correctly, most Werewolf fans were very angry that no thought was given whatsoever to the impact to their game line.<br /> <br /> The best solution is just to ignore the entire Revised era metaplot of every WoD game line. None of it has aged well. They didn't do the other game lines justice. They didn't serve their own game line well either.<br /> <br /> If there's a particular idea(s) in the Revised era that seems interesting to you, feel free to explore it in your own chronicles. Otherwise just ignore the whole thing like a bad potato you ate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T07:17:53-07:00","id":1488691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488670#post1488670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were ignored because at that point in time the Revised developers had segregated each game line in their own silos. Crossover was now a dirty word. Vampire didn't care at all what would impact the Werewolf game. It only cared about that Baba Yaga was a vampire and thus owned by Vampire. That &quot;story&quot; in Nights of Prophecy was meant as an FU to Werewolf and announce that any crossover was over. If I remember correctly, most Werewolf fans were very angry that no thought was given whatsoever to the impact to their game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was an overreaction to the fan reaction to Time of Thin Blood and the Week of Nightmares which went full gonzo with crossovers cumulating with the Technocracy and Kuei-jin killing Ravnos. Fans of the various gamelines got mad about having the gameline's metaplot involve major crossovers so White Wolf decided to pull back on those. I can sympathize but I think White Wolf was mistaken to move Baba Yaga out from being a Werewolf villain and into being a set piece in Vampire who's only role was to get one-shot in order to try and build hype for the Niktuku.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T07:42:51-07:00","id":1488693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488624#post1488624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my main gripes with some people who criticize Haight (beyond the fact that I love to play the &quot;Devil's Advocate&quot; lol) is that some of the criticism he got from some people I knew, imply that a &quot;recurring villain&quot; is somehow a bad thing for the setting and I'm of the complete opposite idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are completely right, and that should be obvious. But this is the thing with such situations, characters like Haight grate on our skin and then we start trying to explain why they're so awful and it's easy to inadvertently blame aspects that are obvious, but not the actual reason.<br /> <br /> It is a lot like the whole &quot;Mary Sue&quot; concept: people try to build lists of Mary Sue traits and diagnosis of Mary Sue characters, but actually the problem is just that the story is badly written and the character comes out as unconvincing. Likewise, Haight has a lot of traits attached to him that became synonymous with bad character, but they're not actually the cause of him being bad, we just try to avoid another Haight.<br /> <br /> Haight is a bad character for three reasons that aren't visible traits of him. Actually, they're not characteristics of the NPC whatsoever:<br /> <br /> 1 - Things happen around him with cheap storytelling. The problem isn't that they happen just to give him power or something, but that the writer makes a bad, lazy job at trying to convince the reader that they're organic happenstances;<br /> <br /> 2 - His presentation is completely geared for the ST, not the players, which results in adventures that make him seemingly pull stuff out of nowhere. The players don't know about his plans, about his powers, about his contacts, they get no hints to any of those before or after the facts, so they only see Haight coming out of nowhere, make some impossible shit up, and leave;<br /> <br /> 3 - Worse of all, <b><u>all</u></b> of his pre-W20 appearances are railroad adventures where his fate has little to no possible input from the players. Every single one of them has a scripted ending accompanied by a huge amount of instructions for the ST to sabotage or outright impede any and every PC action that may result in things not going by the script, <b>and to not stop Haight even after because he'll appear again in an official book</b>.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Ur-Shulgi isn't a bad character because he can't be written well. He's a bad character because he's writing in such a way that he pulls shit out of nowhere, destroy the setting by waving his pinkie and shows less personality than a chair. <b>And all of those can be solved</b>. But solving then won't change the impact of the failings in his initial depiction. See that <i>Lore of the Clans</i> already goes a long way improving him with very little effort, but unfortunately has to do so by retcon. Curiously, <b>not by retconing the character itself as far as anyone can tell, but retconing the bad story itself instead</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488636#post1488636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sam Haight is just one guy</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved your ideas for <b>Pentex</b> as a crossover villain, but I disagree that Haight couldn't do the job.<br /> <br /> Haight could have done it, even doing everything he did in the other adventures, if the above problems were addressed. #1 is the hard part and would require serious rewriting, so lets leave it alone and just assume better writing for his shenanigans. #2 being addressed means players would be given more info and agency during the adventures, and be able to engage with Haight's story and actions even if not always with the man himself. And #3 would mean that interacting with him have actual stakes on the setting.<br /> <br /> A major aspect of dealing with a recurring villain in an RPG is that you must actually do his job and prepare ahead of time for the plans the players may come up with, so his escape doesn't feel forced, and give the players something for their effort, so even if the villain escapes his next appearances show the lasting impacts of the previous ones. But above all, you must be prepared for an untimely demise.<br /> <br /> Now, just imagine if every adventure after the <i>Valkenburg</i> simply had a side box telling you how Haight's exploits cause ripple effects or inspire people, in such a way that if Haight has died before, you can exchange him here <i>with his legacy</i>. Followers, copycats, offended parties trying to recoup their losses or going insane with the repercussions of his actions. You could have all the same stories being told with different characters whose actions are a direct result of the life of Samuel Haight, or just with the man as long as he actually manages to live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488647#post1488647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To Grandmother's House really should have been a Werewolf adventure and involved the PC's helping to lead the shapeshifters and other supernatural creatures of Russia in murdering the hell out of her and her Zmei.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> The bigger problem with her ending is less that it was a Worf Effect for a thing that wouldn't even stay around to impact the setting in any way (although this is a huge sore point), but that the module itself unceremoniously makes the PCs into passive witnesses to the story of Baba Yaga and &quot;Vasilisa&quot;. Few if any module depowered the PCs so thoroughly, and that has nothing to do with splat.<br /> <br /> I think her demise should be a crossover book, because she touched every splat. It should be something anyone can witness or even cause. And instead of making the PCs lead the charge that kills her, the story itself should shift focus to her forces, to the many things her presence and actions cause in the land and why that's everyone's problem. And let the PCs have lasting effects on the setting by their actions, not because they killed her (or failed), but because their actions will shape the aftermath of her fall, the power balance and the size of the leftover threat.<br /> <br /> With this, getting hints of the Nictuku and maybe having a hand in its finding and murdering the Hag would be fine. The scene of her death would be a symbol of the changes they brought instead of the actual purpose of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T09:40:18-07:00","id":1488714,"title":"","content":"If you don't look at details (and you shouldn't, VTM writers really know how to ruin a good thing) , many of these characters have great functions<br /> <br /> Haight created the skin dancers, who are far and away one of the most exciting werewolf enemies because they could be anyone and they really poke hard at the inevitable systemic inequality of Garou and Kinfolk. Haight himself doesn't matter much.<br /> <br /> If you look at Ur-Shulgi, he's the straw that broke the camel's back. A powerful methuselah rises at the right time and turns tensions into war. Now WW1 would've started without the death of the Archduke, and the schism was going to happen without ur-shulgi, but there are still unique benefits to the way it was done with Ur-Shulgi<br /> -His age, experience and direct line to Haqim legitimizes the loyalist faction, the path of blood, and the web of knives as the OGs. Without such a figure, it would be difficult to discredit and disperse the schismatics and justify the purge of influential leaders as anything other than treasonous.<br /> -He's a sorcerer. He's certain to temper the worst of the warriors and ensure that loyalist Sorcerers and likely viziers will be treated well by the warriors who sometimes question their position in the clan. He's a good choice for bridging together the most extreme loyalists and the more centrist elements of the sect. <br /> <br /> <br /> -Cracking the Tremere curse... Ok, I think this is a problem for the players that want Assamites under the Tremere curse. Perhaps it could be retconned as a partial uplifting of the curse. After all, the Assamite Antitribu avoided the Tremere curse, I don't think it's a stretch if some Schismatics avoid the removal of the curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T13:23:02-07:00","id":1488731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but actually the problem is just that the story is badly written and the character comes out as unconvincing </div> </div> </div>This, exactly. It's the most important problem in my view. As I said before, I don't really see any problem in him having access to Gifts, Disciplines and Spheres, as I don't think it's a problem, he's an antagonist after all, I wouldn't even mind if in addition to that he had access to Changeling's Arts lol, but the real problem is that his stories, the way he acquired his powers, etc, were terribly written. It came out as unconvincing at best. Plot armor and all can work wonders if the story is well-written, his character sheet is not the main problem, as stated. It's the story that matters the most. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The best solution is just to ignore the entire Revised era metaplot of every WoD game line. None of it has aged well. They didn't do the other game lines justice. They didn't serve their own game line well either. </div> </div> </div>I'll have to agree with that, most things <i>Revised</i> did were terrible. It would be a much better approach to try to fix the problems the setting had, than the approach they chose. Systematically, it's also bad in most points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think her demise should be a crossover book, because she touched every splat. It should be something anyone can witness or even cause </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would have been great if it happened this way. Such a great opportunity to make a great story. I think she was made into a good and convincing antagonist, her arc deserved a cross-over scenario book, to deal with her and all her allies. Even now, I see myself using Rage Across Russia here and there, it surely had the potential to be the crossover story the setting needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T14:17:24-07:00","id":1488735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488670#post1488670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were ignored because at that point in time the Revised developers had segregated each game line in their own silos. Crossover was now a dirty word. Vampire didn't care at all what would impact the Werewolf game. It only cared about that Baba Yaga was a vampire and thus owned by Vampire. That &quot;story&quot; in Nights of Prophecy was meant as an FU to Werewolf and announce that any crossover was over. If I remember correctly, most Werewolf fans were very angry that no thought was given whatsoever to the impact to their game line.<br /> <br /> The best solution is just to ignore the entire Revised era metaplot of every WoD game line. None of it has aged well. They didn't do the other game lines justice. They didn't serve their own game line well either.<br /> <br /> If there's a particular idea(s) in the Revised era that seems interesting to you, feel free to explore it in your own chronicles. Otherwise just ignore the whole thing like a bad potato you ate.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, it always felt like Vampire would be flipping the bird to any and all other gamelines. It was the darling and the one that got the most love, and they were sure as hell using all the other lines to play Worf to show off how Vampire was ending horribly and cracking along its seams.<br /> <br /> I'd however contest the point that nothing in Revised was any good. Werewolf in general was pretty interesting, with a load of new developments, hopeful unions and the shifters getting off their collective assess and actually trying to make a change - War for Egypt, Purge of the messed up camps, unification efforts in Europe and USA, Ahadi... Some of the best Tribe Books and Breed books were out with Revised, and the mature level of telling tales about Garou that went into a lot of the Revised era sourcebooks was quite refreshing (Hammer and Klaive, Book of Auspices, Possessed). This is of course the End Times part of the plot nonwhistanding, most of that was just random stuff forced by the need to end things.<br /> <br /> I would especially like to single out Apocalypse as a great book, though, even if I'm not very likely to ever use it, and it manages that by mostly ignoring all the other End Times bullshit and inventing is own stuff.<br /> <br /> And as much as I loathed the core setting and metaplot developments of Mage Revised, it did some very clever stuff - I'd like to single out the Rogue Council, Dead Magic 2, Lost Paths and the Tradition books as some excellent material that made things more interesting and was easy to use even if you didn't care for the Revised metaplot. Rogue Council was an especially good gimmick for the age old question newbies had... &quot;What do Mages actually do?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T20:55:45-07:00","id":1488759,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> here, while the full <i>end of time metaplot package</i> was a bad idea, Revised was also the source of a lot of good material.<br /> <br /> Personally I think of it as a new stage of growth for both the setting and its communities of fans and developers. Quality of writing and mechanics largely improved, despite some serious hiccups. Not perfect, but a far better and more stable average than the wild days of 2nd edition, specially early 2nd. A lot of improvements were made, a lot of corrections that worked more often than not, a lot of excellent supplements and some very good modules.<br /> <br /> Revised is as much <i>To Grandmother's House </i>and <i>Lair of the Hidden</i>, the culmination of the changes brought by late 2nd Edition, with the writers dismissing crossover and &quot;gonzo&quot; concepts as they learned to focus and think through their stories. The game we have today owns too much to Revised for the whole edition to be dismissed, even if you want to dismiss its metaplot's development towards the end.<br /> <br /> End, by the way, that was also a part of this. It's easy to look back with current eyes and see how to fix the game of them for the tastes of now, but the reality at the time was that White Wolf had in their hands a game that was broken, and ever more obviously so. And the fact that it can be fixed now doesn't change that they didn't thought so back then. They experimented with mechanics in other games and learned what was wrong with the setting, but for them the construct of WoD was too big to be fixed from within. Not that anyone has to agree with their conclusion (I don't, even for the period) or like what the metaplot did in Revised, but I think it's always important to keep things in perspective by considering their reasons, and that destroying the setting was the plan since 1998.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:15:16-07:00","id":1488823,"title":"","content":"I am running a Chicago y Night chronicle started in 1992 and it is now 1997. The girl who plays a Tremere Seer does not know any story or lore aside from that she as gotten in-game and the other players are very careful not to share anything with her off-game.<br /> She is very curious and has a strong dislike for the Tremere antitribu. So the next session wll start with her getting a vision aout the conlagration of the antitriu as something that is about to happen.<br /> <br /> She has also gotten a a feeling of dread with a forshadowing aout chains that will break, and the emergence of Ur-Shulgi (without nowing what it is aout and who it is). But she loves to try to learn more lore. So slowly Ur-Shulgi will break the curse and she will have an ncling what it is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:28:13-07:00","id":1488837,"title":"","content":"I didn't realize how bad Sam Haight is. Yes I think he exceeds Ur-Shurgi in bad ideas for story telling in a beloved game setting<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. So on a related note to the posters here.<br /> <br /> How would you improve on making Ur-Shurgi more interesting and giving him something akin to a personality?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:31:56-07:00","id":1488850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488837#post1488837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you improve on making Ur-Shurgi more interesting and giving him something akin to a personality?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tho' he is a 4th Generation and old as dirt... he could have a personality<br /> I mean, Mithras, Dracon, Yorak, Antonius and so and so on, almost every 4th Gen have some shreads of personality<br /> Usually I go with the nofficial material that was removed from the final version of Clanbook: Assamite Revised. Ur-Shulgi was Embraced by Haqim in a strategic maneuver to unite the disparate Baali into a regular army, so that they could be destroyed in open combat. The text says that, in order to accomplish this feat, Haqim Embraced a boy \u2013 a ten-year-old shepherd \u2013 who was born with a soul already destined for corruption, and threw him into the sacrificial pit that Saulot said had spawned the original Baali. Something happened to the neonate in that foul place, and through his powerful Cainite blood, the infernalists finally got the leader they needed to assault the Second City en masse. It is told that the Assamite Antediluvian was off in one of his mysterious disappearances, but made it back to the Second City just in time to stop his childe, the new Shepherd of the Baali, and tear the demon out of the body that it rode. When the battle was over Haqim claimed that he had found the boy dying on the battlefield and the Embrace was the only way to save that innocent victim. However, the taint within Ur-Shulgi's soul never vanished and changed that Cainite into something more, and something less<br /> While it opens up the possibility an Assamite version of the Baali 're-embrace&quot;, explain why Ur-Shuligi's childe Al-Ashrad lack of the traditional black skin<br /> And as an extra, gives some &quot;personality&quot; to Ur-Shulugi; I mean if you have born with a soul already destined for corruption... that is a treasure trove of possibilites, a bit like letting a player to have Dark Fate. Sure Ur-Shulugi became what he is, but that not means he never tried to fight against his own Fate just during the millenium, his soul literally slowly erroded away.<br /> I know it a bit clich\u00e9, but Ur-Shulugi is like Anakin Skywalker in this story<br /> A potent boy, who became something horrible, but maybe a glimmer of hope to save him.<br /> The whole devotion to Haquim is a mask, and after learning the truth from a Demon or a Baali, or from Haqim himself, he started to hate his Sire and could be secretly an ally for the Sabbat (actually in my version it was Ur-Shulugi who &quot;protected&quot; the Antitribu of the Sabbat from the Tremere Cure, becasue they truned against the Clan already and joined an organization with the goal of killing the Antediluvians. And allowing the curse was a punshiment for the Haqim-loyalists... after they leraned their lesson, he official awoke and broke the curse on them and started to reform the Clan)<br /> Sometimes give him a little delusion he is the reincarnation of Abel, the Sheperd, who destined to turn to the Dark Side like his bro' Caine<br /> To be honest when I use him, always figure out something to make him an active player, like Michael or Mithras, not just a statue like presence in a dark cave (okay, used that one once., but gave him veins pulsing with greenish hellfire colour and empty eyesocets, glowing with similar eeerie hellfire green light. He was what remained when a Baali used the Level 9 Daimonin power to let something horrible in to the world, he was the gate who was left open, and had to be &quot;shut&quot;. It was a bit silly story, but we had a lots of fun)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-02-2022, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T13:08:43-07:00","id":1488874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488464#post1488464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's plenty of worse ideas but I almost dread bringing them up.<br /> <br /> I mean...<br /> <br /> Himmler of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had mercifully forgotten about that mistake. I have to wonder what were the authors of that book were thinking when they came up with that idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T13:45:58-07:00","id":1488877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488874#post1488874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had mercifully forgotten about that mistake. I have to wonder what were the authors of that book were thinking when they came up with that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Germany = Nazi vampires<br /> <br /> Nazi vampores = Bad<br /> <br /> Sabbat = Bad<br /> <br /> Nazis in Sabbat = Good!<br /> <br /> Which, I follow the (incredibly bad) logic (sort of) but its not just Himmer but Herman Goering too. It's a bit like Nixon and Kissinger both being vampires and joining the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It's horrible and tasteless but also just plain WEIRD to find horrifically infamous world leaders as vampires running around as Sabbat pack members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-