 soon as he got up because he's that good, but because he's reckless and don't know better.<br /> <br /> None of those things need to make him less intelligent, but contextualize his actions and puts this intelligence in perspective, he is smart to an extreme, but he has glaring awareness gaps that are hard for an adult to make sense of. Which sometimes just plays in his favor anyways, because makes him unpredictable, but in the end it isn't a strength and won't work always.<br /> <br /> I personally thing as a personality that's enough. The rest is to make this apparent for the reader and play its consequences, so not all of his actions seem just pure badassery, but also quirks and some miscalculations that arise from his failings. Have him make decisions that are reflexes of who he is, his mental strengths and limitations, what is important to him and what isn't, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you mean, making him like Nicolai from CbN. That would work, Nicolai is an awesome character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T22:24:23-07:00","id":1489057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1488878#post1488878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes (as in, times where Nazis are NOT involved) weird can be fun. Example; Wod's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rasputin&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Rasputin</a>, who seemingly walked so Sam Haight could run.<br /> <br /> The crazy old monk was allegedly one of <i>everything</i>. Though I suppose no WoD said you couldn't kill him because he has to appear in future books, so there was that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find Rasputin hilarious, and his return in Beckett's Jyhad Diary tantalizing and clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T12:56:42-07:00","id":1489915,"title":"","content":"I've never heard of anyone hating Ur-Shulgi. I don't understand this new trend of people shitting on high level characters just because they're powerful. I always thought people liked having Methuselah's/Antes around just to provide that appropriate atmosphere of grandiose history, and the apocalyptic doom that makes being a vampire such a crappy experience. Without them, being a vampire isn't so bad, imho, all you've got to worry about are those pesky residual feelings of guilt from when you were a mortal, and maybe the beast if you're a total savage. I've never played V5 and I don't know much about it tbh (rules wise), so I'm coming from a V20 perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:37:49-07:00","id":1489923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1489915#post1489915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard of anyone hating Ur-Shulgi. I don't understand this new trend of people shitting on high level characters just because they're powerful. I always thought people liked having Methuselah's/Antes around just to provide that appropriate atmosphere of grandiose history, and the apocalyptic doom that makes being a vampire such a crappy experience. Without them, being a vampire isn't so bad, imho, all you've got to worry about are those pesky residual feelings of guilt from when you were a mortal, and maybe the beast if you're a total savage. I've never played V5 and I don't know much about it tbh (rules wise), so I'm coming from a V20 perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been people shitting on high level characters just because they're powerful since the dawn of the game, it's not a new trend.<br /> <br /> But you should avoid making assumptions and blanket statements about the reasons of other people, that's pretty offensive. Maybe some people hate him just because he's a boring, badly written character and that has nothing to do with him being a powerful Methuselah (something the game has enough of without him).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:23:32-07:00","id":1489940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488463-is-ur-shurgi-the-most-hated-in-vtm-or-is-there-competition?p=1489915#post1489915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard of anyone hating Ur-Shulgi. I don't understand this new trend of people shitting on high level characters just because they're powerful. I always thought people liked having Methuselah's/Antes around just to provide that appropriate atmosphere of grandiose history, and the apocalyptic doom that makes being a vampire such a crappy experience. Without them, being a vampire isn't so bad, imho, all you've got to worry about are those pesky residual feelings of guilt from when you were a mortal, and maybe the beast if you're a total savage. I've never played V5 and I don't know much about it tbh (rules wise), so I'm coming from a V20 perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most people don't like this character as he is one dimensional and was meant to be a disposable character that heralded the end of the series twenty some odd years ago. With VTM back and Gehenna being retooled you have a meth that serves no real purpose anymore and to quote Black Fox is a wrecking ball to the game setting.<br /> <br /> There is plenty of ancients in the game that have way more fleshed out personalities and are more interesting like Vykos, Montano, Dracon, and even Mithras to name a few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-12-2022, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}